INSERT INTO "v8_fsqca_v7_1_ese_tests" VALUES('• High-ESE membership exists for only two cases (IND 0.90, ZAF 0.97): ESE·REE defines a distinct, non-European energy–mineral pathway — sufficiency 0.959, i.e., where energy stress and mineral dependence coincide, sovereignty loss is near-guaranteed.','','','');
INSERT INTO "v8_fsqca_v7_1_ese_tests" VALUES('• ~ESE appears in four of five European paths: Europe loses substrate sovereignty WITH comparatively sound electricity systems — the binding constraints are mineral, connectivity, hydrological, and market, not energetic. This converts the ''energy: silent multiplier'' section from a disclosure into a finding.','','','');
INSERT INTO "v8_fsqca_v7_1_ese_tests" VALUES('• The Gulf bloc (ARE, BHR, QAT, SAU) and IDN/MYS lack ESE coverage: the energy–mineral pathway claim cannot yet be tested where it is a priori most plausible. Recorded as the residual EPIS scope.','','','');
