INSERT INTO "v8_theoretical_memo" VALUES('Integrity Principles','1. NO existing data was overwritten without documentation. All new columns (F,G,W,X) are additive.
INSERT INTO "v8_theoretical_memo" VALUES('═══ CSovE MODULE — CARBON SOVEREIGNTY EXPOSURE (v6.4 Extension) ═══','','','','');
INSERT INTO "v8_theoretical_memo" VALUES('CSovE Definition','Carbon Sovereignty Exposure (CSovE) measures the epistemic gap between what a sovereign actor officially claims about its carbon trajectory (NDC pledges under UNFCCC Paris Agreement) and what independently verified data shows (satellite emissions tracking + carbon market integrity). CSovE is the carbon-specific operationalisation of the Epistemic Sovereignty Gap — the core thesis construct — applied to a new physical planetary domain.','','','');
INSERT INTO "v8_theoretical_memo" VALUES('QESIS+ Integration Weight','CSovE_GAP is integrated into the QESIS+ framework at 12% weight, equivalent to CRD. Formula: QESIS_EXTENDED = QESIS_Theory × 0.88 + CSovE_GAP × 0.12. The existing five-dimension QESIS_Theory score (WSE·CSE·ODI·CRD·REE) is preserved intact. QESIS_EXTENDED is an additive extension, not a replacement.','','','');
INSERT INTO "v8_theoretical_memo" VALUES('Sub-indicators','CSovE_CLAIM (0-100): NDC ambition deficit — 40% trajectory gap (Climate Watch) + 60% CAT credibility discount (CAT ordinal 1-6). CSovE_VERIFY (0-100): Real substrate gap — 40% ClimateTRACE underreport factor + 35% ICVCM offset integrity deficit + 25% World Bank governance deficit. CSovE_GAP = (CLAIM + VERIFY) / 2. Higher score = larger epistemic distance.','','','');
INSERT INTO "v8_theoretical_memo" VALUES('Tier Classification','INFR (75-100): Maximum epistemic sovereignty gap. Underreport factor >2.5 or no carbon governance. Applies to E-AU fossil states: BHR, SAU, QAT, KWT, OMN, RUS, IRN, MEX. EPIS (50-74): Significant gap, partial governance. Most A-EU developing economies: IND, IDN, JPN, KOR, BRA, ZAF, POL. ACTIVE (0-49): Active pricing mechanisms, verified trajectories. EU core + NOR + SGP + AUS: DEU, FRA, CHE, NOR, GBR, NZL, SGP.','','','');
INSERT INTO "v8_theoretical_memo" VALUES('Cathedrical Code Mapping','CSovE_CLAIM → Axis 3 (Hermeneutics) / Imaginary / SYMBOLIC_ASSERTION: state performing carbon sovereignty it cannot audit. CSovE_VERIFY (ClimateTRACE) → Axis 2 (Phenomenology) / Real / SUBSTRATE_RUPTURE: satellite-verified physical reality the Symbolic cannot contain. CSovE_VERIFY (ICVCM) → Axis 2 (Phenomenology) / Real / SUBSTRATE_RUPTURE: offset market integrity failures as physical ruptures. CSovE_VERIFY (World Bank) → Axis 4 (Metaphysics) / Symbolic / Pragmatics: governance infrastructure for internalising the Real. CSovE_GAP → Axis 7 (Epistemology) / Binary Integrity Guard: the arithmetic gap IS the Epistemic Sovereignty Gap.','','','');
INSERT INTO "v8_theoretical_memo" VALUES('Key Events (fsQCA corpus)','Frankfurt Climate Ruling Aug 2025: SUBSTRATE_RUPTURE event for NDC pledges. Kariba scandal 2023 / Shell fraudulent projects Dec 2025: ICVCM offset integrity ruptures. US withdrawal from Paris Agreement Jan 2026: live SYMBOLIC_ASSERTION collapse. These are coded as SUBSTRATE_RUPTURE events in Table2_Discourse (n=15).','','','');
INSERT INTO "v8_theoretical_memo" VALUES('Data Sources','CSovE_CLAIM: UNFCCC NDC Registry (unfccc.int/NDCREG); Climate Watch WRI (climatewatchdata.org, CC BY 4.0); Climate Action Tracker (climateactiontracker.org). CSovE_VERIFY: Climate TRACE v5.4 (climatetrace.org, CC BY 4.0); ICVCM Assessment Status Dec 2025 (icvcm.org); World Bank Carbon Pricing Dashboard Aug 2025 (carbonpricingdashboard.worldbank.org). Coverage: 35 countries. Reference year: 2024. BIG flag threshold: <75% field coverage.','','','');
INSERT INTO "v8_theoretical_memo" VALUES('═══ LACANIAN–fsQCA STRUCTURAL BRIDGE (Chapter 2 Architecture) ═══','','','','');
INSERT INTO "v8_theoretical_memo" VALUES('OVERVIEW','The Hilbert-Lacanian Vector Space H_LSI = H_R ⊗ H_S ⊗ H_I provides the formal substrate linking psychoanalytic registers to empirical fsQCA conditions. Each register maps to a physical constraint operator and a set of observable fsQCA codes. The non-commutativity [Ô_sym, Ô_rup] ≠ 0 mathematically proves that states cannot simultaneously maximize symbolic claims and minimize real physical stress.','','','');
INSERT INTO "v8_theoretical_memo" VALUES('H_S — SYMBOLIC REGISTER / SYMBOLIC_ASSERTION','Maps to: Regulatory operator Ô_sym.
INSERT INTO "v8_theoretical_memo" VALUES('H_R — REAL REGISTER / SUBSTRATE_RUPTURE','Maps to: Physical constraint operator Ô_rup.
INSERT INTO "v8_theoretical_memo" VALUES('H_I — IMAGINARY REGISTER / IMAGINARY_PROJECTION','Maps to: Imaginary coherence operator — the mirror-stage projection of frictionless sovereignty.
INSERT INTO "v8_theoretical_memo" VALUES('SYNTHESIS: THE EPISTEMIC SOVEREIGNTY GAP AS ENTANGLEMENT','The tensor product H_LSI = H_R ⊗ H_S ⊗ H_I is non-separable (proven by QCT Frobenius norm = 1.041, entanglement ratio = 0.515 > 0.2 threshold). This means Real, Symbolic, and Imaginary registers are entangled — a country cannot have a purely Symbolic position without Real and Imaginary components leaking in. The Epistemic Sovereignty Gap (ESG) IS the off-diagonal density matrix term ρ_RS — the quantum coherence between Symbolic claim and Real substrate that cannot be zeroed out through better regulation alone. CSovE_GAP operationalises ρ_RS for the carbon domain. The Lindblad dissipation term D[ρ] describes how this coherence decays under environmental decoherence (conflict, fiscal stress, geopolitical rupture) measured by γ_n = CONFLICT×0.40 + FISCAL_STRESS×0.35 + GEOPOL_RISK×0.25.','','','');
INSERT INTO "v8_theoretical_memo" VALUES('BIG GATE — GAP B RESOLUTION','The 14 QESIS+ countries missing CSovE scores (CHL, HKG, TWN, ISR, BEL, USA, ESP, FIN, AUT, CAN, NLD, SWE, DNK, ITA) are NOT a methodological flaw. They trigger the Binary Integrity Guard (BIG) protocol — Axis 7 (Epistemology) of the Cathedrical Code. When field coverage < 75%, BIG forces EPIS status to prevent false-precision ranking.
INSERT INTO "v8_theoretical_memo" VALUES('WTO VS WEF CITATION RESOLUTION (Gap C)','Two distinct metrics capturing different regimes of the same deglobalisation phenomenon:
