Conditions (k=6): WSE · CABLE [CSE_COMPOSITE] · REE · HYPER [TeleGeography corridor %] · ESC_inv · GCI_inv.
Key config A: ~WSE·~CABLE·REE·HYPER·ESC·GCI → DEU/AUT/CHE "Arendtian paradox": highest-governed states, structurally stateless in physical infrastructure.
Key config B: WSE·CABLE·REE·HYPER·ESC·GCI → SGP/ARE/ISR "Conjunctural totalisation": all vulnerability axes present.
Key config C: WSE·~CABLE·REE·HYPER·~ESC·~GCI → BHR/SAU/QAT "Physical trap": water-REE double bind, Foucault: infrapower without infrastructure.
Calibration: Theory-driven direct method (Ragin 2008), anchored to Aqueduct tier boundaries and QESIPE weight thresholds.
Thresholds: Consistency ≥ 0.80 · Coverage ≥ 0.60 · PRI ≥ 0.75.','','','');
Conditions (k=5): PARL_RES · EXEC_DISC · INVEST · LEGAL_ACT · CHOKE_AWR.
Anchor: EU Parliament P10_TA(2026)0022 (22 Jan 2026) = full membership (1.0) for PARL_RES.
Anchor: Draghi (2024) "too late for EU to develop challengers to major US cloud providers" = 0.5 crossover for EXEC_DISC (acknowledges dependency, commits to nothing).
Anchor: FISA §702 (2023) — Biden admin cited EU digital dependence as intelligence advantage → USA EXEC_DISC = 0.95 (hegemonic producer of the dependency discourse).
Anchor: Von der Leyen mission to Virkkunen (2024): unified "tech sovereignty, security, democracy" portfolio → EU institutionalised sovereignty discourse.
Foucauldian frame: political speech IS the dispositif — not merely describing sovereignty but constituting it.
Validation: Krippendorff α ≥ 0.70 inter-coder reliability required before DPhil submission.','','','');
Conjoint conditions (k=4):
  WSE⊗REE: both water AND REE vulnerability — cannot be independently mitigated (Bell inequality violation analogy)
  CABLE⊗HYPER: cable presence BUT hyperscaler-owned — more cables = more dependency (entangled state)
  GCI⊗~ESC: high digital capacity + low structural sovereignty = governance-infrastructure gap
  Δ_WSE_2050: climate decoherence trajectory (Aqueduct 2050 pessimistic minus baseline)
Theoretical foundation: Lindblad master equation dρ/dt = -i[H,ρ] + Σ(LᵢρLᵢ† − ½{Lᵢ†Lᵢ,ρ})
  H = dominant structural force (hyperscaler capital, water stress)
  Lᵢ = dissipative channels (cable concentration, REE dependency, regulatory capture)
  ρ = sovereign infrastructure density matrix — MIXED state for all 35 countries
DPhil original contribution: first operationalisation of Lindblad non-separability in sovereign infrastructure analysis.','','','');
  State space: 6-dimensional QESIPE vector per country
  Action space: policy interventions (cable diversification, domestic REE, GCI, ESC)
  Reward function: reduction in QESIPE decoherence toward resilient archetype
  Transition function: fsQCA causal paths identify which state combinations reliably reach low-vulnerability outcome
fsQCA as policy-state encoder for sovereign infrastructure RL = DPhil Chapter 5 original contribution.','','','');
Weight rationale: EMODnet weighted 0.6 as validated peer-traceable source; SCM 0.4 fills geographic gap.
Used in: QESIPE+ base formula (col W).
Documented limitation: non-EU countries use SCM-only → CSE_COMPOSITE reflects different construct for EU vs. non-EU. Must be disclosed in thesis methodology chapter as first-order approximation of the composite observable.','','','');
Problem: Additive GCI increases QESIPE+ for DEU (GCI=97.9), FIN (GCI=100), DNK (GCI=100). This is theoretically wrong: Germany''s high digital governance IS NOT additional vulnerability — it is its only mitigating factor. Treating GCI as a vulnerability axis conflates "measuring risk" with "being at risk."','','','');
Formula','QESIPE+ = (WSE×0.28 + CSE_COMP×0.28 + ODI×0.165 + CRD×0.085 + REE×0.16) × (1 + GCI_inverse×0.08)
where GCI_inverse = 1 − GCI/100

Base weights sum to 1.00: WSE 0.28 + CSE 0.28 + ODI 0.165 + CRD 0.085 + REE 0.16 = 1.00
Multiplier range: GCI=100 → multiplier=1.000 (no amplification); GCI=0 → multiplier=1.08 (max 8% increase).

Intentionally modest multiplier (max 8%): GCI is a moderator, not primary driver. Physical infrastructure axes dominate.

Examples:
  DEU (GCI=97.9): multiplier=1.002 → minimal — governance nearly offsets vulnerability modifier
  BHR (GCI=97.9): multiplier=1.002 → same multiplier, but extreme physical exposure dominates score
  HKG (GCI=N/A→0): multiplier=1.080 → max amplification — no cybersecurity data signals higher decoherence risk','','','');
QESIPE+ (col W) is a NEW parallel column, not a replacement. Full backward compatibility preserved.
Readers can track formula evolution: QESIS Theory → QESIS+ Base → QESIPE+.','','','');
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
QESIS Theory      | 0.350 | 0.350 | 0.200 | 0.100 |  —    | absent          | 1.00
QESIS+ Base       | 0.298 | 0.298 | 0.170 | 0.085 | 0.150 | absent          | 1.00
QESIPE+ v6.1      | 0.280 | 0.280 | 0.165 | 0.085 | 0.160 | ×(1+inv×0.08)   | 1.00

Progression: WSE+CSE share gradually declines as additional axes added. REE increases (USGS 2024 China 68.6% confirms). GCI shifts from axis to moderator — architectural maturation reflecting deepening theoretical understanding.','','','');
— Draghi, The Future of European Competitiveness, Sep 9 2024
Use: 0.5 crossover for EXEC_DISC. Acknowledges dependency, commits to nothing. Foucault: surrender of counter-conduct at executive level.','','','');
— P10_TA(2026)0022, European Parliament, 22 January 2026
Use: Full membership anchor for PARL_RES. Most comprehensive tech sovereignty resolution. Arendt: rights acknowledged without substrate.','','','');
— Mission letter to Henna Virkkunen, 2024
Use: EU INVEST=0.85, LEGAL_ACT=0.95. Sovereignty institutionalised at executive architecture level.','','','');
